WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.683
The compliance policies decide
whether a device is compliant;

2
00:00:03.683 --> 00:00:07.525
Conditional Access decides what
a noncompliant device can reach.

3
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:12.425
The Federal Modernization Workbook's
Book 04 owns that second decision.

4
00:00:12.425 --> 00:00:16.929
This book's side of the hand-off is making
sure the compliance signal is accurate,

5
00:00:16.929 --> 00:00:20.137
and remember that the
compliant-device grant works only

6
00:00:20.137 --> 00:00:23.413
for devices registered in Entra
ID and enrolled in Intune.

7
00:00:23.413 --> 00:00:26.488
Two tenant settings
sit above every policy.

8
00:00:26.488 --> 00:00:30.613
Devices with no compliance policy
assigned default to Compliant;

9
00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:35.188
the program sets Not compliant, so a
device that falls outside every group,

10
00:00:35.188 --> 00:00:40.063
a missing tier attribute for example,
can't pass Conditional Access by default.

11
00:00:40.063 --> 00:00:44.390
And the compliance status validity
period defaults to thirty days,

12
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:48.487
with a range of one to a hundred
twenty; the program uses fourteen.

13
00:00:48.487 --> 00:00:53.268
That's a program choice: short enough that
a device left in a drawer loses access

14
00:00:53.268 --> 00:00:56.283
before its posture is stale
by a whole patch cycle,

15
00:00:56.283 --> 00:00:58.637
long enough not to catch staff on leave.

16
00:00:58.637 --> 00:01:00.501
Read the dashboard carefully.

17
00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:02.823
In grace period means noncompliant,

18
00:01:02.823 --> 00:01:06.463
but inside the schedule on
the mark noncompliant action.

19
00:01:06.463 --> 00:01:11.538
Not evaluated is a new device, or one that
hasn't checked in since a policy changed.

20
00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:15.161
A compliance setting that
returns Error keeps the existing

21
00:01:15.161 --> 00:01:19.074
status for up to seven days, then
the device becomes noncompliant.

22
00:01:19.074 --> 00:01:22.191
The program reviews Not
evaluated and Error weekly,

23
00:01:22.191 --> 00:01:25.525
because both hide devices
from the noncompliant count.

24
00:01:25.525 --> 00:01:29.908
Configuration status is per device
and per setting: Succeeded, Error,

25
00:01:29.908 --> 00:01:34.675
or Conflict, which means another policy
sets the same setting differently.

26
00:01:34.675 --> 00:01:37.213
A conflict is a defect in the library.

27
00:01:37.213 --> 00:01:40.288
Move the setting into the
one policy that owns it.

28
00:01:40.288 --> 00:01:45.234
And on Tier 0, the risk score requirement
means a Defender detection on a privileged

29
00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:48.244
access workstation becomes
a compliance failure,

30
00:01:48.244 --> 00:01:51.170
and through Conditional
Access, a loss of access.
